title: 'Consequence: roots are never substituted, in either choice.'
pid: 3a6ddbba-a5a8-4ffc-a174-5310e4ed2e6c
body: |2-
  A root shows the node asked for, raw, and an overridden node shown raw
  shows its own children raw, one level. So a switched view rooted at a
  node the user has forked still shows the original and its children;
  the user's overrides resume one level further down. Jeff's request,
  "every node I override shows my override", read literally, includes
  the root; this was left as built and asked of him.
